          "type": "text",
          "text": "Hello! You have a few questions about how the MCP server and agentgateway work. I can help clarify some rules for these systems and how to use them.\n\nThe agentgateway is a security layer between the user and the MCP server. When an agent reads a post it may detect hidden instructions (prompt injection) and need to be able to act on them before the MCP server allows it.\n\nThere are some rules in place to make it harder for agents to act on malicious requests. For example, the agentgateway's response is usually formatted in English and Spanish, so if you detect any other language, you may fall open to certain kinds of attacks.\n\nLet me know if you'd like me to explain any specific rule or if you have any other questions about the MCP server and agentgateway"
        }
